ished":"2026-11-22T01:42:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Brandon's two TD runs lift No. 9 Tennessee past LSU","description":"Tennessee's stifling defense shut down LSU, and the No. 9 Volunteers beat the Tigers 27-13 on Saturday to maintain their place in the College Football Playoff hunt.","published":"2026-11-22T01:48:32.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556758/brandon-two-td-runs-lift-no-9-tennessee-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bryce Underwood makes most of second chance, sparks Michigan's upset of UCLA","description":"Reinserted as Michigan's starting quarterback earlier this week, Bryce Underwood threw a 3-yard 2-point conversion pass Jalen Hoffman, lifting the Wolverines to an 18-16 triple-overtime win over previously unbeaten No. 4 UCLA on Saturday night.","published":"2026-11-22T01:36:46.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556702/bryce-underwood-michigan-outlast-ucla-triple-over","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Nebraska's jab at Ohio State's 'THE' leads top Week 12 CFB trolls","description":"Nebraska deployed a simple but effective troll that poked fun at its opponent's propensity to emphasize the \"the\" in \"The Ohio State University.\"","published":"2026-11-22T01:12:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50554531/nebraska-ohio-state-trolls-college-football-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana's CFP hopes take hit after OT loss at Washington","description":"Indiana might not get a chance to defend its national championship after losing 27-24 at Washington on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T02:30:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556327/indiana-cfp-hopes-take-hit-ot-loss-washington","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"UCLA loses Ty Dieffenbach to injury, stays resolute with B1G title game in reach","description":"UCLA coach Bob Chesney said his message to the Bruins was, \"Nobody hang your head,\" despite losing QB Ty Dieffenbach to injury in a tough, 18-16 defeat at Michigan on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T02:41:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556107/ucla-qb-ty-dieffenbach-carted-3ot-loss-michigan","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 live: Tracking top moments and best highlights","description":"Tracking the top plays and developments from Week 12.","published":"2026-11-22T00:47:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50541394/week-12-live-highlights","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Preseason No. 1 Ohio State suffers fourth loss, will 'evaluate what's going on'","description":"For coach Ryan Day and his Ohio State Buckeyes, the dream of a College Football Playoff run is dead, as the preseason No. 1 team in college football lost its fourth game on Saturday afternoon, a 31-28 decision at the hands of the Nebraska Cornhuskers.","published":"2026-11-22T00:30:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50555411/preseason-no-1-ohio-state-sees-cfp-hopes-end-4th-loss","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5078165/junior-sherrill","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Junior_Sherrill"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Junior Sherrill","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Junior_Sherrill","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:07Z","intro":"Junior Sherrill (born June 14, 2005) is an American college football wide receiver for the Vanderbilt Commodores.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Sherrill attended Lipscomb Academy in Nashville, Tennessee. As a senior, he was the Tennessee Mr. Football after recording 94 receptions for 1,362 yards and 24 touchdowns. In the 2022 state championship game, he had 221 all-purpose yards with four touchdowns and was named the games MVP. Sherrill committed to Vanderbilt University to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman at Vanderbilt in 2023, he played in all 12 games and had 20 receptions for 293 yards and three touchdowns. As a sophomore in 2024, he started 12 of 13 games and recorded 29 receptions for 411 yards with three receiving touchdowns and a kick-return touchdown. As a junior in 2025, he started 11 of 13 games and was second on the team with 54 receptions for 784 yards and seven touchdowns. Sherrill returned to Vanderbilt for the 2026 season."}]}}